            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41324",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "basic-ftp: basic-ftp: Denial of Service via unbounded memory growth from malicious directory listings"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "basic-ftp is an FTP client for Node.js. Versions prior to 5.3.0 are vulnerable to denial of service through unbounded memory growth while processing directory listings from a remote FTP server. A malicious or compromised server can send an extremely large or never-ending listing response to `Client.list()`, causing the client process to consume memory until it becomes unstable or crashes. Version 5.3.0 fixes the issue."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41324",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-41324\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: basic-ftp\nFixed Version: 5.3.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-41324](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41324)\nbasic-ftp is an FTP client for Node.js. Versions prior to 5.3.0 are vulnerable to denial of service through unbounded memory growth while processing directory listings from a remote FTP server. A malicious or compromised server can send an extremely large or never-ending listing response to `Client.list()`, causing the client process to consume memory until it becomes unstable or crashes. Version 5.3.0 fixes the issue.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-41324**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|basic-ftp|5.3.0|[CVE-2026-41324](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41324)|\n\nbasic-ftp is an FTP client for Node.js. Versions prior to 5.3.0 are vulnerable to denial of service through unbounded memory growth while processing directory listings from a remote FTP server. A malicious or compromised server can send an extremely large or never-ending listing response to `Client.list()`, causing the client process to consume memory until it becomes unstable or crashes. Version 5.3.0 fixes the issue."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
